@@ -24,6 +24,31 @@ input throws `InvalidTaskError`, which carries the position of the first
 invalid item in `index`. All library errors extend `TaskPlanError` and have a
 `code`.

+## Planning
+
+`planOrder` computes an execution order and stages for validated tasks. It
+throws `DuplicateTaskError` for duplicate ids, `UnknownDependencyError` for
+missing dependencies, and `CycleError` for cycles.
+
+```ts
+import { planOrder } from "./src/index.ts";
+
+const result = planOrder([
+  { id: "a", dependsOn: [], priority: 0 },
+  { id: "b", dependsOn: ["a"], priority: 0 },
+]);
+console.log(result.order.join(", "));
+```
+
+You can also run the planner from the command line:
+
+```
+node src/cli.ts plan tasks.json
+node src/cli.ts plan tasks.json --json
+```
+
+See `examples/basic.ts` for a runnable example.
+
 ## Development

 Requires Node.js 24 or later. TypeScript files run directly with Node.
